  "source":"Appendix AD-1; Appendix I-65/I-66 Table 060; Section 12.39 Segment 155 (12-96 through 12-99); Elements 2 and 12 (13-25,13-31,13-32)",
  "applicability":"Bounded parsed-field account-updater request/response and follow-on credential profile; not a First Data eligibility engine or full wire parser.",
  "sourceNotes":[
    "AD requires participating acquirer, CNP and COF/installment/recurring context. Merchant registers and certifies with First Data; secure account storage is part of the definition. Issuer/acquirer participation and actual qualification require external evidence.",
    "Participating merchants should send Table 060 sub-table 01 on installment, recurring and COF requests. First Data determines qualification; updates are supplied only when available.",
    "Table 060 allows up to 100 data bytes. Sub-table headers are two-digit ID and length, ranges 01-25, with 1-25 alphanumeric data bytes. Only 01 and 02 have specified semantics here.",
    "01 has length 01, Y (all updates) or I (indicators only). 02 has length 01, O (do not perform optimization). 01/02 are mutually exclusive; Visa/MasterCard CNP Auth/Sale/Refund only.",
    "If 01 is omitted, no update information is returned even if optimization occurs. O is an explicit opt-out; reconcile its use with AD all-request guidance instead of inventing a mandatory Y-only policy.",
    "Segment 155 is sent only when the transaction qualifies for and uses First Data Auth Optimizer. Tables have three-digit ID/length and are not separated by field separators; unpopulated fields are omitted.",
    "155 tables 001 updated PAN and 002 updated TransArmor token allow up to 19 alphanumeric bytes, only with Y and Visa/MasterCard; 001 is excluded for TransArmor and 002 excluded for PAN transactions.",
    "155 table 003 expiry is four-byte YYMM with Y, Visa/MasterCard. Table 004 is A/E/Q/C/U with Y/I, Visa/MasterCard. Do not infer that status A makes every update field mandatory.",
    "155 table 005 original association decline requires Y/I, Visa/MasterCard and network decline followed by optimizer-directed reattempt. Its length description 3 conflicts with data maximum 4; bounded data is checked, exact width reviewed.",
    "155 table 006 has six-byte result code and Y/I, Visa-only. Fifteen listed values VAU001-VAU014 and VAU016 are recognized; VAU015 is not listed. Reasons do not independently certify network eligibility or transaction approval.",
    "Elements 2/12 permit original or updated PAN/TransArmor token on follow-ons, with corresponding expiry. Updated response expiry uses YYMM; parsed manually entered Element 12 expiry uses MMYY.",
    "Retry of a follow-on reversal, completion, cancellation, void of merchandise return or timeout reversal retains the credentials from its initial attempt. Logical token values are not complete TAP requests."
  ],
